You can see that Irene cheered up.
"Now we can sleep with no worry! My father said we may not fear predators, while we are in caves."
"Well, perhaps..."
This cave is a good shelter, which can protect you from the dangers of the forest of the night; the only thing that bothers you is the open entrance. 

It's getting dark outside very soon. In a few hours you can hardly recognize objects at arm's length, the rest is hidden in impenetrable darkness. You are all tired and scared. The jungle outside is filled with strange and frightening sounds. Some animals scream and howl in the thicket, weird rustles can be heard all the time. No wonder you can't fall asleep in such circumstances.
Suddenly, forest animals begin to scream especially loud. You can hear some small, rapid animals climbing up the trees. It seems that a large predator is approaching.
To your horror you hear rustle of moving branches, and see sparkling eyes of a predator, who is breathing loudly. You've got to do something, before it's too late.